{
 "example": "display-a-popup-on-hover",
 "note": "Nine places across Washington with a marker each, and a popup the page builds in the DOM rather than in the map, so what a fixture can compare is the markers. They are what this one is for: nine copies of an added image over a dense basemap at zoom 11.15, two of them close enough to overlap, drawn with `icon-allow-overlap` so neither is dropped. It reads 13. Checked rather than assumed, since a fixture near the base's own number could as easily mean neither renderer drew the layer: against a base-only frame the markers come to 8769 pixels, the same 8769 on both sides. It writes `icon-allow-overlap` where the page writes `icon-overlap`, which the pinned oracle predates and refuses the layer for.",
 "base": "https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/bright",
